  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This is a work of formidable narrative architecture. The book's power lies in its commitment to grounding the 1952 polio crisis in the precise, dated material reality of the hospital—the weight of an iron lung, the specific timestamp of a turning point—which builds an unshakable sense of immediacy. Its multi-track structure honors the event's logistical and physiological complexity without resorting to simplistic heroism, a discipline maintained even in the aftermath. However, this impressive control can, at times, feel overly procedural. A subtle but persistent mechanical rhythm in its senten",
